# client.js and default-opencues.md are BUILD ARTIFACTS THAT ARE COMMITTED.
#
# That is deliberate and it is the opposite of what this repo does everywhere
# else (integrations/chrome/dist/ is not committed). The reason is specific to
# this ecosystem rather than a change of principle:
#
# The dsh plugin marketplaces install by CLONING the repository and running
# `npm install --omit=dev --ignore-scripts`, with scripts disabled BY DEFAULT
# for safety. So `prepublishOnly` never runs on that path, and a gitignored
# bundle simply would not exist — the node half would load, the config route
# would answer, and nothing would ever paint or fill. Their own installer
# says as much when it falls back: "using the build artifacts committed in
# the repo".
#
# Staleness is the cost of committing derived output, and it is guarded:
# `scripts/check-dsh-bundle-fresh.sh` rebuilds and diffs (esbuild is
# byte-reproducible for identical inputs), and runs in pre-pr.sh + CI.
#
# So: if you change anything under src/, run `pnpm --filter @opencues/dsh
# build` and commit the result alongside it.
